    "title": "Proposed creation of new zoning designation supported by Pittsylvania County officials - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shannon Kelly ,\n1 hours ago Local officials have proposed the creation of a new heavy industrial zoning district for the Berry Hill megasite, formally known as the Southern Virginia Megasite. In a called meeting held at noon Tuesday, Dec. 30, Pittsylvania County Board of Supervisors members approved advertising a proposal that would amend the county’s zoning ordinance to create a new, special heavy industry zoning district, different from the existing M1 and M2 – light, and heavy industrial zones, respectively. This change would apply to the Berry Hill megasite, and, according to county staff and supervisors, is designed to accommodate specific anticipated developments there. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
